  "id": "regulatory-behavior",
  "term": "regulatory behavior",
  "definition": "Regulatory behavior refers to an infant’s characteristic way of managing emotion and interaction during the still-face setting. In this research context, it is described in patterns such as mainly positive social engagement, persistent distress that is hard to soothe, or reliance on self-comforting actions.",
